In one of the first five amber novels (the name of the right one escapes me) 
Corwin travels to Tir-Na Ni-Goth (forgive me if the spelling is wrong) 
Amber's 'shadow in moonlight' where the future can be seen.  There he 
encounters his elder brother Benidict's image and Grayswandir is the weapon 
he uses to fight this image's mechanical arm (for some reason it can touch 
him.)  I've always thought of this as the inspiration for the Hallucination 
resistance effect of the artifact in NH.

Also, as Grayswandir has the image of the pattern etched on it's blade (in 
part) one could point to the great power of order that this represents and 
say that is why.

